volkdude85 edition, and a placeholder that asks nothing
======================================================

Onboarding said "GitHub edition", which names the host rather than the thing. It says **volkdude85
edition** now — lowercase, because the handle is lowercase on purpose and setting it in caps would
undo the only reason the spelling matters. The kicker lost its `text-transform: uppercase` for that
reason; nothing else on the screen changed.

The composer placeholder was "You gonna talk to me or what?", which is a line from somebody's
conversation rather than an instruction. It says **Text goes here…** now — the same information, with
no register to live up to on a screen where somebody is deciding whether to type.

